  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Voices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Detailed description of the activity The goal of the project is to provide Georgian minority citizens with accurate and reliable information in order to enable them to, on the one hand, make informed decisions and opinions, and on the other hand, help them avoid disinformation. The project will: - Provide content grants (12,000 GEL each media outlet) and editorial support to six minority media. (8 journalistic materials per media outlet). - Simultaneously, the project&#x2019;s external editors &#x2013; media experts and seasoned editors - will work with the newsrooms in their local languages to improve their use of multimedia tools and approaches. - Face-to-face, broadcast and online town-halls with politicians will be organized by partner media outlets, in which ethnic regional media journalists will collect concerns and aspirations from local communities, reframe these issues into questions and pose them to local and national politicians. - Support media literacy campaign by providing a pool of 24,000 GEL to two Georgia-based media-literacy organizations, who are already successfully engaging Georgian-speaking citizenry to expand and adapt their activities to include minority communities.</narrative>
  </description>
